# Never copy a node_modules folder from the build machine into an image.
#
# Every Dockerfile installs its own dependencies with `pnpm install` and then
# copies source with `COPY packages/ ...` / `COPY . .`. Without this file those
# COPY steps also copied the server checkout's own node_modules (left over from
# a manual install on 2026-04-13) ON TOP of the freshly installed ones. When the
# 2026-11-10 lockfile change renamed the @langchain/core install directory, the
# stale symlinks pointed at a directory that no longer existed and the worker
# crash-looped on "Cannot find module '@langchain/core/output_parsers'" for
# ~33 hours. See CLAUDE.md, production quirk #10.
**/node_modules
